A useful exact refinement has emerged. On the normalized generic fiber, the polar summand is
\[
a_\gamma=-\operatorname{ord}_\gamma(dg/j)-1.
\]
Thus pole ends contribute \(+\delta_\gamma\), finite ends contribute \(-\kappa_\gamma\), and adjunction gives only the signed identity \(\Delta_\infty-K_\infty=2-2g-s\). This exposes why genus/polar class cannot bound the local positive part: finite-end contact is the compensating term. I’m also deriving the precise internal telescope for the higher Smith torsion lengths; the remaining question is whether any proved map carries that telescope to \(n_P\).
